# Build context for the images under deploy/docker: debuglet.Dockerfile,
# which builds the role images from the release payload, and
# provisioner.Dockerfile, which builds the deployment provisioner.
#
# The context is the repository root and deliberately keeps .git: the
# packaging tool reads the revision from it and refuses a modified checkout.
# Everything listed here is generated locally, is ignored by git, and is not
# part of the source the payload is built from. No tracked file matches any of
# these patterns, so a clean checkout still builds.

.cache
.ci
.data
.venv
.DS_Store
deploy/certs
deploy/dist
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Operator material that a working tree is expected to hold and that must
# never reach an image layer: the inventories and pinned host identities that
# name private infrastructure, the certificates the deployment and the local
# compose rig use, and captured traffic.
deploy/ansible/hosts.yml
deploy/ansible/hosts.dev.yml
deploy/ansible/known_hosts
deploy/ansible/known_hosts.dev
deploy/docker/nginx/certs
local/configs/dispatcher/server.crt
local/configs/dispatcher/server.key
local/configs/executor/client.crt
local/configs/executor/client.key
**/*.crt
**/*.key
**/*.pcap
